WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.813
Zones and conduits turn risk analysis into architectural boundaries.

00:00:03.813 --> 00:00:08.765
A zone groups logical or physical assets that share security requirements based

00:00:08.765 --> 00:00:10.828
on factors such as function,

00:00:10.828 --> 00:00:12.891
criticality, consequence, ownership, and exposure.

00:00:12.891 --> 00:00:16.191
A zone should represent a meaningful trust decision,

00:00:16.191 --> 00:00:19.080
not merely an existing subnet or room.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:22.793
A conduit is a controlled communication path between zones.

00:00:22.793 --> 00:00:29.394
It carries the data and services that the operation requires while enforcing the boundary's security expectations.

00:00:29.394 --> 00:00:33.520
Teams should document approved sources, destinations, protocols, direction, purpose, users,

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:34.758
and administrative ownership.

00:00:34.758 --> 00:00:40.535
For example, an enterprise reporting system may need production data from a site historian.

00:00:40.535 --> 00:00:44.661
That requirement does not justify direct enterprise access to controllers.

00:00:44.661 --> 00:00:49.612
An intermediary service in an industrial DMZ can replicate required data while

00:00:49.612 --> 00:00:52.087
reducing reachability toward lower-level control functions.

00:00:52.087 --> 00:00:56.213
Zone design should distinguish systems with different risk and capability.

00:00:56.213 --> 00:01:00.339
Safety functions, control areas, engineering services, remote access, wireless devices,

00:01:00.339 --> 00:01:03.228
and legacy equipment may warrant separate treatment.

00:01:03.228 --> 00:01:06.941
Conduits should also account for administration, updates, backups, authentication,

00:01:06.941 --> 00:01:10.242
and vendor support, not only routine production traffic.

00:01:10.242 --> 00:01:13.130
Segmentation technology implements part of the design,

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:17.256
but a firewall alone does not create a defensible zone.

00:01:17.256 --> 00:01:21.382
The boundary needs current inventory, documented flows, secure configuration, monitoring,

00:01:21.382 --> 00:01:23.032
ownership, and change control.

00:01:23.032 --> 00:01:27.983
Teams must also test that restrictions preserve timing, redundancy, failover, and recovery.

00:01:27.983 --> 00:01:31.697
Review zones and conduits when architecture or risk changes.

00:01:31.697 --> 00:01:34.585
Cloud analytics, new vendors, temporary maintenance links,

00:01:34.585 --> 00:01:39.124
and production expansions can introduce paths that bypass the intended model.

00:01:39.124 --> 00:01:41.187
The objective is necessary, limited,

00:01:41.187 --> 00:01:44.900
observable communication between assets with clearly understood trust relationships.
